      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "4. By means of this writ petition, the petitioner has challenged the order dated 07.11.2023, passed by Collector/D.M./Land Acquisition-respondent no.4 by which, application of the petitioner for reference to the appropriate Authority has been rejected on its being delayed.\n5.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 521,
      "end": 797,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "07.11.2023",
          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 602,
          "end": 612
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": false
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013 (for short \"Land Acquisition Act,\n2013\") is a beneficial piece of legislation and it has been held by the Hon'ble Apex Court in the case of Collector Land Acquisition Anantnag and another Vs. MST. Katiji and others, reported in AIR 1987 SC 1353, which is recently followed by Hon'ble High Court of Madhya Pradesh in Writ Petition No.1952 of 2017, whereby it has been declared that since the Land Acquisition Act, 2013 is a beneficial piece of legislation and in that case the provision shall be construed in favour of the oustees in case of any doubt.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 798,
      "end": 1508,
      "entities": [
        {
